                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e16256c-4788-3595-914f-386fa94b23fc",
                                        "entry_id": "a854249e-22d7-396d-ab6d-7f21f2d65117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The identity element, neutral element."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3fb772f-c69f-40e3-b464-8c19c95bca4f",
                                                "sense_id": "9e16256c-4788-3595-914f-386fa94b23fc",
                                                "text": "An element 𝑒 of 𝑆 such that 𝑒𝑥 = 𝑥 = 𝑥𝑒 for all 𝑥 ∈ 𝑆 is called a unit element. (When the law of composition is written additively, the unit element is denoted by 0, and is called a zero element.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfcc5746-cacb-3671-a8eb-d2b4504285dc",
                                        "entry_id": "a854249e-22d7-396d-ab6d-7f21f2d65117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An element having an inverse, an invertible element; an associate of the unity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "493e643a-bf41-4a5e-b419-862de40f7b4d",
                                                "sense_id": "cfcc5746-cacb-3671-a8eb-d2b4504285dc",
                                                "text": "Let 𝐴 be an arbitrary integral domain. We say that an element 𝑎 ∈ 𝐴 is invertible or is a unit of 𝐴 if it has an inverse in 𝐴; in ℤ the units are ±1, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd326702-239f-36b1-9083-9c09d72d529e",
                                        "entry_id": "a854249e-22d7-396d-ab6d-7f21f2d65117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an adjunction, a natural transformation from the identity functor of the domain of the left adjoint functor to the composition of the right adjoint functor with the left adjoint functor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e8167c1-c02c-37e9-b12e-643cafd06e04",
                                        "entry_id": "a854249e-22d7-396d-ab6d-7f21f2d65117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A volume of rock or ice of identifiable origin and age range that is defined by the distinctive and dominant, easily mapped and recognizable petrographic, lithologic or paleontologic features (facies) that characterize it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "067b77f1-f269-44f3-835c-9fd90e28dd29",
                                                "sense_id": "3e8167c1-c02c-37e9-b12e-643cafd06e04",
                                                "text": "For example, the Moenkopi Formation was named for the small settlement of Moenkopi, Arizona where the formation was first defined as being a separate unit from the rocks above and beneath it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
